<title>USA: Fed adds reserves via overnight system repurchases.</title>
<headline>Fed adds reserves via overnight system repurchases.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve added temporary reserves to the banking system on Tuesday through overnight system repurchase agreements, a New York Fed spokeswoman confirmed.</p>
<p>Fed funds were trading at a soft 5-3/16 percent at the time of the operation, below the Fed's 5-1/4 percent target for the rate.</p>
<p>Some analysts had thought that the Fed would refrain from operations on Tuesday.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1679</p>
